            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
          %blockquote
            %p more details, and more polishing later…
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+of+bundle+gerbes"} transgression of bundle gerbes
          %h2#references References
          %p The classical notion of transgression of forms through fiber bundles is described in section 9 of
          %ul
            %li#Borel
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Armand+Borel"}> Armand Borel
              ,
              %em Topology of Lie groups and characteristic classes
              Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. Volume 61, Number 5 (1955), 397-432. (
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.bams/1183520007"}> EUCLID
              )
          %p
            Transgression as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+in+cohomology"} pullback in cohomology
            along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation+map"} evaluation map
            followed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
            over the base space is considered in:
          %p
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              , §3.5 in
              = succeed "," do
                %em Loop Spaces, Characteristic Classes, and Geometric Quantization
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-8176-4731-5"} doi:10.1007/978-0-8176-4731-5
          %p
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            (and with an eye towards defining the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
            of
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes+with+connection"} bundle gerbes with connection
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernesto+Lupercio"}> Ernesto Lupercio
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernardo+Uribe"} Bernardo Uribe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Holonomy for Gerbes over Orbifolds
                %strong 56
                (2006) 1534-1560 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0307114"}> arXiv:math/0307114
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geomphys.2005.08.006"} doi:10.1016/j.geomphys.2005.08.006
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (over
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+B%C3%A4r"}> Christian Bär
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Becker"} Christian Becker
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Characters and Geometric Chains
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Characters
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 2112
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.6457"} arXiv:1303.6457
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-07034-6_1"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-07034-6_1
          %p
            Transgression of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+groups"} discrete groups
            to cohomology of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inertia+groupoids"} inertia groupoids
            (see at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+in+group+cohomology"} transgression in group cohomology
          %ul
            %li#Willerton08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Willerton"}> Simon Willerton
                , Section 1 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The twisted Drinfeld double of a finite group via gerbes and finite groupoids
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0503266"} arXiv:math/0503266
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Tu"}> Jean-Louis Tu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ping+Xu"} Ping Xu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The ring structure for equivariant twisted K-theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0604160"} arXiv:math/0604160
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/CRELLE.2009.077"} doi:10.1515/CRELLE.2009.077
            %li#AdemRuanZhang07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Adem"}> Alejandro Adem
                ,
                = succeed "," do
